  "2026-11-05T16:56:32.426Z",codex-agent,"npm run release:check passed with isolated HOME and disabled global/system Git configuration: 444 tests passed, zero failed/canceled/skipped; all 49 source files reported. Coverage is 100% statements/lines (8013/8013), functions (403/403), branches (3862/3862); zero duplication, 1127 documented declarations, zero production vulnerabilities and 192-file pack dry-run passed. Artifact shasum: 8b19100a815ea9a354f1b16107d908519c8d4d74. Strict read-only PM health passed with zero warnings. No timeout retries were needed. Bun release gate is running serially next."
  "2026-11-05T16:56:34.944Z",codex-agent,"Final regression structure proof rerun after removing duplicated fixture setup: original command and broad timeout-code matcher each fail the respective targeted child test (the runner counts both child and parent as failures: 1 pass, 2 fail); original guide yields 1 pass and 1 fail. Restored implementation and guide pass all 5 focused tests. All mutation proofs used disposable copies; the package worktree retained the fixed implementation."
  "2026-11-05T17:05:00.259Z",codex-agent,"bun run release:check also passed at unchanged thresholds: 444 tests passed, zero failed/canceled/skipped; all 49 sources at 100% statements, lines, branches and functions. npm and Bun both produced the same 192-file pack dry-run shasum 8b19100a815ea9a354f1b16107d908519c8d4d74. Both full gates passed on their first run with no timeout retries. All 10 linked PM test commands passed. No PM CLI/SDK defect was found; configured test-result tracking is disabled and comments preserve results. Both unresolved review findings are fixed; no thread replies, resolutions, mentions, merge or release were performed. Final source, rebuilt dist and append-only PM evidence are ready for orchestrator verification; pushed-head CI is tracked on https://github.com/unbraind/pm-jev/pull/92/checks."
  "2026-11-05T17:44:01.314Z",codex-agent,"Round 7: fetched all 13 review threads and every comment without pagination gaps; exactly two unresolved: PRRT_kwDOU8IMzs60MMXi (npm JavaScript entrypoint discovery) and PRRT_kwDOU8IMzs60MMXZ (per-decision no-mutation scope). Latest CodeRabbit review has no outside-diff findings. Both verified valid. Remote head 8c1f4b8 already includes main. Plan installation-derived, file-verified npm/npx entrypoints with POSIX and win32 fixtures, scoped guide regression, disposable-copy behavioral reverts, whole-diff same-class review, and serial unchanged npm/Bun release gates."
  "2026-11-05T17:47:23.581Z",codex-agent,"Implemented round 7: npm/npx JavaScript entrypoints now come from a valid absolute npm_execpath sibling or the active Node installation, with file checks and a clear install/remediation refusal; PATH shims are never consulted. Fixtures cover POSIX bin/lib, win32 sibling layouts, npm caller paths, requested CLI selection, missing/directory entries and literal arguments. Guide now scopes inference/mutation refusal to the current decision and explicitly retains earlier backlog updates. Whole-PR same-class review checked changed runners, admission call sites, CLI documentation and guarantees; the docs-install caller was updated to stop passing PATH, and no further instance required a change."
  "2026-11-05T17:47:35.491Z",codex-agent,"Behavioral revert proofs in a disposable package copy: fixed control runs 2/2 passed. Reverting only npmInvocation and its original imports to 8c1f4b8 makes the default-runtime native-PATH-shim/no-npm-caller regression fail 0/1 with Cannot locate the installed npm JavaScript entry point (no injected-signature mismatch). Restoring only the original guide makes the per-decision guarantee regression fail 0/1 with ERR_ASSERTION. Restoring both fixes reruns 2/2 passed. The source worktree was never mutated for either revert. Initial focused runner/docs tests passed 7/7; the linked expanded runner/docs/packed-install command passed 10/10 with zero failures or skips. Test-result storage is disabled by project policy; these comments retain receipts."
  "2026-11-05T17:50:24.797Z",codex-agent,"Out-of-scope dependency audit follow-up: pm-jev-dev-glob-cancellation records three moderate development-toolchain findings through c8/test-exclude/glob for GHSA-3g3m-2fjr-6pw4. Exact-advisory search found no duplicate; the previous closed braces-chain item tracks different advisories. No dependency pins or gate thresholds changed in this review round."
  "2026-11-05T18:10:38.922Z",codex-agent,"Round 7 npm release gate PASSED on the fixed code with unchanged thresholds: npm run release:check; full suite 448 passed, 0 failed/canceled/skipped, duration 785517 ms. All 49 inventoried sources reached 100 percent statements/lines/functions/branches (8013/8013 statements and lines, 403/403 functions, 3862/3862 branches). Typecheck, lint, zero duplication, build, release identity/privacy, 1127 documented declarations, production audit (zero vulnerabilities), 192-file pack dry-run (shasum 59b9f422f7631068ec3262c82a2706295fcc2e94), changelog and publish-attestation checks passed. The gate used an isolated home, disabled global/system Git configuration, a minimal credential-free child environment, and no more than two test workers. No timeout retry was needed. Dist was rebuilt and remains byte-identical. Bun full gate is running serially after npm."
  "2026-11-05T18:14:03.653Z",codex-agent,"Round 7 Bun release gate PASSED: bun run release:check; full suite 448 passed, 0 failed/canceled/skipped, duration 652510 ms. Identical unchanged 100 percent coverage on all 49 sources (8013 statements/lines, 403 functions, 3862 branches), zero production vulnerabilities, and the same 192-file pack dry-run shasum 59b9f422f7631068ec3262c82a2706295fcc2e94 as npm. All static, build, identity/privacy, docstring, duplication, changelog and publication-attestation checks passed. Both full gates passed on the first attempt; no host-load timeout retry was needed. The focused linked command passed 10/10. Behavioral reverts each failed 1/1 and fixed/restored controls passed 2/2 in disposable copies. Releasing this agent claim while leaving the item in progress for orchestrator verification; the dependency follow-up remains open. Review threads remain untouched. Final tracker writes precede fresh pushed-head CI verification."
